Estimate the annual fuel savings due to the weight reduction provided by composites in a fleet of 50 767 aircraft owned by a commercial airline. Assume a weight saving of 570 kg per aircraft and an annual fuel saving of 830 l per year per kg of weight saved.
Express the answer in this unit: \mathrm{l}

Before the final answer line, give a concise worked solution with the governing equation, substitution with units, and the calculation.

Given that the density of $\mathrm{Cu}_{2} \mathrm{O}$ is $6.00 \mathrm{Mg} / \mathrm{m}^{3}$, calculate the Pilling-Bedworth ratio for copper.

\[
\begin{aligned}
\text{Atomic weight of copper:} \quad & M_{\mathrm{Cu}} = 63.55 \;\mathrm{g/mol} \\
\text{Atomic weight of oxygen:} \quad & M_{\mathrm{O}} = 16.00 \;\mathrm{g/mol} \\
\text{Density of copper metal:} \quad & d_{\mathrm{Cu}} = 8.93 \;\mathrm{Mg/m^3} \\
\text{Density of } \mathrm{Cu_2O}: \quad & D_{\mathrm{Cu_2O}} = 6.00 \;\mathrm{Mg/m^3}
\end{aligned}
\]

Before the final answer line, give a concise worked solution with the governing equation, substitution with units, and the calculation.
